// Where the honeycomb rests on each hook, per raw meat (looks only). Generated by tools/hang/honeyrest.py and the
// export step in tools/hang (honey_rest.json); do not edit by hand.
//
// The comb hangs from the hook's smaller curl. Where the meat (or a neighbour's) is in the way it doesn't pass into it
// but comes to rest against it: for each meat on each of the nine hooks, poses around the curl were tried (four ways
// its flat face can point, tilts of 15 to 90 degrees about every level axis in 30-degree steps). Kept: the least of the
// comb inside any meat on a full rack (solid test on a 1 cm grid), then within 2 % of that the pose whose centre hangs
// lowest, as gravity would leave it. Where nothing is in the way the comb still turns a little: its weight isn't under
// its hanging point, so it swings until it is. The four biggest meats keep 9 to 13 % of the comb inside them, all at
// the curl, because that curl is inside the meat.
//
// Pose: rotation (x, y, z, w), size (times the copy's own scale) and position, in the rack's own space.
